/-!
# Pointwise computed-II+ coframe equation of the Dirac-dual root

The nonlinear reduced local family has already been generated and proved
jointly `C¹`.  This module takes its genuine coframe derivative, identifies it
with the existing action-produced `D II+` coefficient, and localizes compactly
supported reduced stationarity to a pointwise equation.  The equation is then
exposed in the explicit first-order EC-shaped balance proved by the preceding
module.

No continuity receipt, field equation, stationary actual, inverse, stress
tensor, or target response is accepted as data.  The terminal four-leg theorem
remains a conditional critical-locus equivalence and does not inhabit that
locus.
-/

